   "subject": "Model Averaging unmarked",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">So, I&#39;m trying to &#39;model average&#39;<div><div>bestmods &lt;- fitList(LEP9, LEP24)</div><div><b>predict(bestmods, type = &quot;state&quot;)</b></div><div>coef(bestmods)</div><div>SE(bestmods)</div><div>lp &lt;- modSel(bestmods)</div></div><div><br></div><div>LEP9 and LEP24 are 2 models that are within AIC delta 2. </div><div>The line of code in bold I (assume?) takes an average of the occupancy estimates of the two models.</div><div>Is this all you can do in model averaging? </div><div>Because I was led to believe that I need to take an average of these models and then use the &#39;averaged model&#39; to generate coefficients and use the averaged model to get the p values for the different covariates.</div><div><br></div><div>So basically, I&#39;m asking is there more to do with model averaging than finding the average occupancy estimates of the occupancy models?</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "UQPxfPPUCgAJ",
   "from": "Richard Chandler",
   "author": "403be63af7ebf220",
   "date": "2019-12-04T12:46:38Z",
   "subject": "RE: [unmarked] Model Averaging unmarked",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Hi Chris,<u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">You can compute model-averaged predictions in ‘unmarked’ (as you did in your code), but you can’t average coefficients. If you want to do the latter, you could use the\r\n ‘AICCmodavg’ package. Just be aware of the pitfalls of averaging coefficients, some of which are described in this paper:\r\n</span></span><a href=\"https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1890/14-1639.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1890/14-1639.1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450800771000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0i4ZReE-LB6xtctfkgOfv_\">https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1890/14-1639.1</a>.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Richard<span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">--<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Richard Chandler<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Associate Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Wildlife Ecology and Conservation<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">University of Georgia<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"tel:(706)%20542-5815\" value=\"+17065425815\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">706-542-5815</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"http://chandlerlab.uga.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://chandlerlab.uga.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450800771000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OWZQsVEmxfcHCYbpQ65t6\"><span style=\"border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0in\">http://chandlerlab.uga.edu/</span></a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\